1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,425
When a cyclist pedals harder the bicycle

2
00:00:02,438 --> 00:00:06,488
travels faster each second Acceleration tells us

3
00:00:06,638 --> 00:00:09,587
how much velocity changes in one second

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,650
We will use a simple example to

5
00:00:11,650 --> 00:00:13,663
find the change in velocity and the

6
00:00:13,662 --> 00:00:14,600
distance travelled

7
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:17,927
Consider an object moving along a straight

8
00:00:17,927 --> 00:00:20,340
line We call its starting velocity v

9
00:00:20,340 --> 00:00:23,477
nought and the time t Acceleration a

10
00:00:23,477 --> 00:00:26,377
measures how much velocity changes each second

11
00:00:26,790 --> 00:00:29,740
With constant acceleration the velocity after t

12
00:00:29,752 --> 00:00:32,277
seconds is v nought plus a times

13
00:00:32,277 --> 00:00:32,614
t

14
00:00:33,051 --> 00:00:36,138
On a velocity time graph distance travelled

15
00:00:36,151 --> 00:00:38,914
relates to the area underneath the graph

16
00:00:39,301 --> 00:00:42,701
With constant acceleration displacement is v nought

17
00:00:42,701 --> 00:00:45,101
times t plus a times t squared

18
00:00:45,114 --> 00:00:48,188
divided by two This is signed displacement

19
00:00:48,638 --> 00:00:51,726
its magnitude equals distance if the object

20
00:00:51,826 --> 00:00:53,213
does not reverse direction

21
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:55,617
A cyclist moves at 2 metres per

22
00:00:55,617 --> 00:00:59,079
second and accelerates at 1.5 metres per

23
00:00:59,092 --> 00:01:02,542
second squared After four seconds the velocity

24
00:01:02,554 --> 00:01:06,054
is 2 plus 1.5 times 4 that

25
00:01:06,054 --> 00:01:08,592
is 8 metres per second The displacement

26
00:01:08,667 --> 00:01:11,530
is 2 times 4 plus 1.5 times

27
00:01:11,530 --> 00:01:14,530
4 squared divided by 2 that is

28
00:01:14,530 --> 00:01:17,792
20 metres Check the average velocity is

29
00:01:17,804 --> 00:01:20,142
5 metres per second so in four

30
00:01:20,142 --> 00:01:22,630
seconds the cyclist travels 20 metres

